<title>BELGIUM: EU says reviews ELG Haniel buy of Rewometaal.</title>
<headline>EU says reviews ELG Haniel buy of Rewometaal.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Friday it was reviewing a proposal by ELG Haniel GmbH, a subsidiary of Franz Haniel &amp; Cie GmbH, to acquire control of the whole of Rewometaal Stainless Processing BV.</p>
<p>It said in a statement the deal was notified for clearance on October 22 under the merger regulation 4064/89. The Commission has about a month to clear the operation or start a full probe.</p>
<p>ELG Haniel is active in industrial recycling and raw material supply.</p>
<p>Rewometaal trades and processes aluminium and copper scrap. It also processes stainless steel scrap, but this aspect falls under the European Coal and Steel Community treaty, the statement published in the November 7 Official Journal C332 said.</p>
<p>There were no other details.</p>
</text>
